1
00:01:22,931 --> 00:01:26,041
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,185
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:01:30,277 --> 00:01:31,478
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله

4
00:01:34,899 --> 00:01:40,032
A few points, final points on the Ghazawat(غزوات) of Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

5
00:01:42,975 --> 00:01:43,971
Number one;

6
00:01:45,011 --> 00:01:52,259
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would command his army generals, the field officers

7
00:01:52,299 --> 00:01:59,672
 not to establish the Hadood(حدود), on the soldiers, when they are in a state of war.

8
00:02:00,418 --> 00:02:07,850
So, the Hadood(حدود) are not to be applied, when it is a state of war.

9
00:02:08,323 --> 00:02:14,430
Because someone might defect and join the Kuffar(كفار)

10
00:02:15,573 --> 00:02:22,103
and that is much worse than not having the Hadd(حدّ) applied on them.

11
00:02:22,716 --> 00:02:30,644
He would also ask his army officers to be accommodating to some of the men

12
00:02:31,164 --> 00:02:36,255
who are helpful in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

13
00:02:37,307 --> 00:02:44,479
However, they might have some mistakes or flaws in their personality or their conduct or their manners.

14
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:55,192
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه he, for example this is a letter that you sent to his leaders, he said;

15
00:02:55,563 --> 00:03:00,775
لَا يَجْلِدَنَّ أَمِيْرُ الْجَيْشٍ وَلَا سَرِيَه، أَحَدًا حَتَّى

16
00:03:01,105 --> 00:03:05,297
يَتْلَعَ دَّرْ لِعَلَّى يَحْمِلُ الشَّيْطنْ عَلى نِيَّه الْحَقَّ بِالْكُفَّارْ

17
00:03:06,278 --> 00:03:06,905
He said;

18
00:03:07,151 --> 00:03:15,494
The Umaraa(أمراء) of the Army's or the detachments, should not lash or flog anyone,

19
00:03:16,486 --> 00:03:18,732
until they come back to their land

20
00:03:19,303 --> 00:03:23,068
because they might defect to the camp of the Kuffar(كفار).

21
00:03:23,972 --> 00:03:31,174
Because I mean some of the punishments are severe, and the person might have fear

22
00:03:31,488 --> 00:03:33,207
and run away and join the Kuffar(كفار).

23
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:36,307
So, it's a general rule,

24
00:03:36,331 --> 00:03:41,479
لَا تَكُوْنُوْ عَوْنَ الِّشَّيْطنِ عَلى أَخِيْكُمْ

25
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:45,637
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Don't help Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) on against your brother.

26
00:03:48,517 --> 00:03:52,520
Don't do anything that would, help Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) on against your brother,

27
00:03:54,517 --> 00:03:56,446
for example the brother did something wrong,

28
00:03:56,501 --> 00:03:58,503
so he became very harsh on the brother,

29
00:03:58,730 --> 00:04:01,498
he becomes defensive, he starts arguing

30
00:04:02,866 --> 00:04:06,386
and by doing that he is siding with Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ),

31
00:04:07,722 --> 00:04:08,275
you see

32
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:16,995
or for example you see someone, who had a very dark history

33
00:04:18,035 --> 00:04:22,816
and now, and they want to repent and they want to join the ranks of the Saliheen(صالحين)

34
00:04:24,248 --> 00:04:27,611
and you start making fun of their past and you make fun of them

35
00:04:28,068 --> 00:04:30,483
and you give that impression that they're not good enough.

36
00:04:30,782 --> 00:04:32,353
So, they say well forget about it.

37
00:04:32,422 --> 00:04:34,977
I'm not going to join you I'm going to go back to my old ways.

38
00:04:35,493 --> 00:04:38,627
So, by doing that you have helped Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) against your brother.

39
00:04:39,617 --> 00:04:43,808
So, one should not help Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) against a Mo'min(مؤمن).

40
00:04:49,368 --> 00:04:59,362
For example, one of his army leaders Salman Al-Rabi'aa Al-Bahli(سلمان ألربيعة ألباهلي),

41
00:05:00,949 --> 00:05:08,237
he had a problem with Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) and Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمروبن معديكرب),

42
00:05:09,339 --> 00:05:13,141
Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمروبن معديكرب) and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي), were two former Murtaddeen(مرتدين),

43
00:05:13,244 --> 00:05:18,314
 not only were they were Murtaddeen(مرتدين) but they were the leaders, of Al-Murtaddeen(المرتدين).

44
00:05:19,022 --> 00:05:22,051
Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمروبن معديكرب) in Yemen and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) in Najd(نجد).

45
00:05:23,178 --> 00:05:27,431
These were the spearheads of the effort of the Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

46
00:05:29,631 --> 00:05:32,212
So, they were the top evil doers.

47
00:05:33,128 --> 00:05:37,166
We're not talking about somebody with middle rank, these were the top ranking Murtaddeen(مرتدين)

48
00:05:38,190 --> 00:05:42,338
and they were men of war, these were skilled fighters with long history of warfare

49
00:05:43,326 --> 00:05:48,244
and because of their pride and skill in fighting,

50
00:05:48,576 --> 00:05:51,547
they rebelled against the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

51
00:05:53,195 --> 00:05:59,132
Later on, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) showed them, the strength and the power of the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

52
00:05:59,204 --> 00:06:04,877
so they gave up and they became Muslim, once again.

53
00:06:08,424 --> 00:06:13,836
So, Suleman Bin Rabiaa Al-Bahali(سليمان ألربيعة ألباهلي), was not treating them well.

54
00:06:14,869 --> 00:06:17,306
He had this problem with Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمروبن معديكرب).

55
00:06:19,322 --> 00:06:24,559
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he sent a letter to Salman Bin Rabi'a(سلمان بن ربيعة).

56
00:06:24,979 --> 00:06:25,979
He said;

57
00:06:26,895 --> 00:06:34,207
فَقَدْ بَلَغَنِيْ صَنِيْعَكَ بِأَمْر وَإِنَّكَ لَمْ تُحْسِنْ بِذَلِكَ وَلَمْ تُجْمِلْ فِيْه

58
00:06:35,012 --> 00:06:42,585
فَإِذَا كُنْتَا بِمِثْلِ مَكَانَكَ فِيْ دَارِالْحَرْبِ فَنْظُرُ أَمْرً وَطُلَيْحَه وَقَرِّبْ هُمَا مِنْكَ

59
00:06:42,764 --> 00:06:47,180
وَسْمَعْ مِنْهُمَا فَإِنَّ لَهُمَا بِالْحَرْبِ وَعِلْمًّا وَتَجْرُبَه

60
00:06:47,644 --> 00:06:53,556
وَإِذَا وَسَلْتَا اِلَى دَارِالسِّلْمِ فَأَنْزِلْهُمَا مَنْزِلَتَهُمَا الَّتِيْ أَنْزَلَ أَنْفُسَهُمَا بِهَا

61
00:06:54,031 --> 00:06:56,098
وَقَرِّبْ أَهْلَ لْفِقْهِ وَالْقُرْآن

62
00:06:56,752 --> 00:06:57,363
He said:

63
00:06:57,689 --> 00:07:03,403
I've received news, of what you have done with Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمروبن معديكرب),

64
00:07:03,919 --> 00:07:05,807
and you have not done well.

65
00:07:06,043 --> 00:07:08,991
The way you treat the Amr(عمرو) is not right, he wasn't treating him well,

66
00:07:09,098 --> 00:07:11,363
he said: The way you're treating Amr(عمرو), is not right.

67
00:07:14,292 --> 00:07:15,205
He said;

68
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:24,261
When you are in a state of war you need to take Amr(عمرو) and Tulaiha(طليحه) and put them next to you

69
00:07:25,428 --> 00:07:27,658
 and have them as advisors for you,

70
00:07:28,471 --> 00:07:32,295
and you need to listen attentively to their advice, their counsel.

71
00:07:32,629 --> 00:07:33,030
Why?

72
00:07:33,054 --> 00:07:36,219
فَإِنَّ لَهُمَا بِالْحَرْبِ وَعِلْمًّا وَتَجْرُبَه

73
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:40,581
Because they are knowledgeable in the field of war and they are experts.

74
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:50,891
However, when you go back to the Land of Peace then put them, where they put themselves

75
00:07:51,641 --> 00:07:54,911
and draw near to you the people of Fiqh(فقه) and Qur'an.

76
00:07:56,132 --> 00:08:00,142
He said: When you go back to the land the peace put them, where they put themselves.

77
00:08:00,717 --> 00:08:01,873
Where did they put themselves?

78
00:08:01,969 --> 00:08:05,104
Because of their Ridda(ردة),

79
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:08,384
and what they have done in the time of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه ,

80
00:08:08,689 --> 00:08:11,681
they have definitely lost some of their status among the Ummah(امة),

81
00:08:12,205 --> 00:08:16,071
because of that stigma of being part of the camp of Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

82
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:20,856
So, he said: When you get back to the land of peace, put them where they deserve to be.

83
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:25,541
And you're not putting them in that status, because you are wronging them,

84
00:08:25,566 --> 00:08:32,482
it is because they are the ones, who have put themselves, in that position because of their actions.

85
00:08:34,467 --> 00:08:35,912
In other words, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying,

86
00:08:35,937 --> 00:08:39,282
maybe they don't need to be promoted to high levels, Amr(عمرو) and Tulaiha(طليحه).

87
00:08:39,756 --> 00:08:42,852
However, in the condition of war,

88
00:08:43,011 --> 00:08:46,989
you need to promote them and make them your personal advisors. Why?

89
00:08:47,253 --> 00:08:49,382
Because they are experts in this field.

90
00:08:50,994 --> 00:08:54,436
Even though, they might not have the best Akhlaaq(أخلاق),

91
00:08:55,466 --> 00:08:57,923
they might not be the most righteous men in the army,

92
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:00,704
they might not have the greatest Taqwa(تقوى)

93
00:09:01,138 --> 00:09:04,199
but when it comes to the field of war, they are the experts.

94
00:09:04,906 --> 00:09:06,809
Therefore, you need to have them close to you,

95
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:09,946
however you don't appoint them in any position of responsibility,

96
00:09:10,117 --> 00:09:11,814
you keep them as a Shuraa(شورى) counsel for you.

97
00:09:13,461 --> 00:09:16,408
When you go back to the land of peace, who would you bring next to you?

98
00:09:17,104 --> 00:09:19,471
The people of Qur'an and Fiqh(فقه).

99
00:09:20,905 --> 00:09:23,325
So, you need to put the right person in the right place

100
00:09:24,510 --> 00:09:28,305
and sometimes a person is suitable for one position,

101
00:09:28,547 --> 00:09:30,864
you transfer him to another he's not the right person.

102
00:09:32,235 --> 00:09:35,204
Amr(عمرو) and Tulaiha(طليحه) are good in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

103
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:41,888
but when it comes to the institutions within the Islamic community.

104
00:09:41,912 --> 00:09:44,329
Like for example, the Imamah(إمامة) and the teaching

105
00:09:44,532 --> 00:09:47,826
and such areas, they're not the right people for it,

106
00:09:50,485 --> 00:09:53,055
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) claim to be a prophet at one point of time.

107
00:09:54,404 --> 00:10:00,796
However now, he deserves to be…. Please brothers, turn off your mobiles…

108
00:10:08,032 --> 00:10:12,737
There's a similar situation that happened in the time of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه.

109
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:22,451
When he was recruiting for the war, either it was, either against Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين)

110
00:10:22,475 --> 00:10:26,893
or against the Persian Empire or the Roman Empire.

111
00:10:26,918 --> 00:10:29,525
Most likely it was against the Persian and Roman Empire.

112
00:10:31,417 --> 00:10:40,636
So, he was recruiting all of these Bedouins and villagers and they would come to Madina.

113
00:10:41,936 --> 00:10:45,426
You see Rasool Allah ﷺ he lived in Makkah and Madina,

114
00:10:46,290 --> 00:10:49,412
he didn't go anywhere else Rasool Allah ﷺ did not anywhere else.

115
00:10:50,391 --> 00:10:56,091
So, the people who benefited from him most are the ones, who chose to be close to him.

116
00:10:57,070 --> 00:10:59,325
The ones who chose to live in Madina

117
00:10:59,765 --> 00:11:04,506
or the ones who were living in Makkah, during the first 13 years,

118
00:11:05,579 --> 00:11:08,787
 or the tribes that were very close to Madina.

119
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:13,783
These are the ones that got the most benefit out of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

120
00:11:14,404 --> 00:11:16,510
but the tribes who are further away,

121
00:11:18,635 --> 00:11:24,224
they didn't received that Tarbiyyah(تربية) that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, who were in Madina received.

122
00:11:25,203 --> 00:11:26,953
You see within the Sahabah(صحابه) you have ranks,

123
00:11:28,532 --> 00:11:32,337
you have the greatest is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and then Umar(عُمَر)

124
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:40,153
and then you have the Council of six which was appointed by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن ألخطاب).

125
00:11:41,851 --> 00:11:45,609
And then you have the Ashra Mubashireen Bil Jannah(عشره مبشرين بالجنة) and the six or among them.

126
00:11:47,337 --> 00:11:49,504
And then you have Ahlul Badr(أهل البدر),

127
00:11:51,059 --> 00:11:52,281
and then after Ahlel Badr(أهل البدر)

128
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:54,473
As'haab Bait Ur-Ridhwan(أصحاب بيت الرضوان)

129
00:11:54,521 --> 00:12:00,694
and these are 1400 Sahabi(صحابي), the ones who gave Rasool Allah ﷺ the Pledge of Allegiance under the lout tree

130
00:12:01,654 --> 00:12:03,726
 and the number was 1400.

131
00:12:04,714 --> 00:12:06,055
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says about them,

132
00:12:06,409 --> 00:12:10,926
لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ

133
00:12:11,378 --> 00:12:15,812
Allah is pleased with the believers who gave you the Pledge of Allegiance under the tree.

134
00:12:16,651 --> 00:12:22,338
And then the next status and the last,

135
00:12:22,822 --> 00:12:28,238
this is the last status are the ones who became Muslim after Fath(فتح) Makkah.

136
00:12:29,844 --> 00:12:35,210
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: The ones who believed after the opening of Makkah

137
00:12:35,429 --> 00:12:38,824
are not equal to the ones who believed before the opening of Makkah.

138
00:12:41,508 --> 00:12:46,913
And these who became Muslim towards the end of the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the last two years

139
00:12:47,413 --> 00:12:49,932
 are Sahabah(صحابه) who maybe only met Rasool Allah ﷺ once,

140
00:12:50,017 --> 00:12:51,962
maybe they only attended one of his talks.

141
00:12:53,431 --> 00:12:56,920
 Maybe the only time they saw him was in Hajjah-Tul-Widaa( حجّةُ الوداع).

142
00:12:59,416 --> 00:13:05,175
So, they are not equal to the Sahabah (صحابه) who spent years and years studying under Rasool Allah ﷺ.

143
00:13:07,385 --> 00:13:15,724
Now, on top of that you have some Taba'een(تابعين), who are from distant lands.

144
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:21,447
So, the level of tarbiyah(تربيعة) was different not everybody had the same tarbiya(تربيعة),

145
00:13:22,045 --> 00:13:23,795
the tarbiya(تربيعة) that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had,

146
00:13:24,107 --> 00:13:28,304
was different than the tarbiya(تربيعة) somebody thousand kilometers away had.

147
00:13:28,506 --> 00:13:31,407
Even though, both were contemporaries of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

148
00:13:33,531 --> 00:13:36,793
So, some of these men are coming into Madina, they were the new recruits

149
00:13:37,915 --> 00:13:41,784
and they didn't have sufficient tarbiya(تربيعة) many of them were not Sahabah(صحابه).

150
00:13:43,753 --> 00:13:45,854
They were new Muslims they just became Muslim,

151
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:51,393
they were coming to Madina responding to the call of Hayyah Alal-Qitaal(حيً ألالّقِتال).

152
00:13:51,417 --> 00:13:55,349
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is inviting them to fight and they came to Madina they're responding to the call.

153
00:13:56,662 --> 00:13:59,839
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in Madina have good Akhlaaq(أخلاق), good manners,

154
00:13:59,864 --> 00:14:04,773
good behavior, they know how to treat others, they're very compassionate, merciful.

155
00:14:05,849 --> 00:14:09,578
But then you have some of these Bedouin tribes coming in and they're rough, harsh.

156
00:14:10,799 --> 00:14:12,581
They lack the Akhlaaq(أخلاق).

157
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:17,217
You know, the Bedouin leads a very tough lifestyle,

158
00:14:17,413 --> 00:14:19,358
 so that reflects on their behavior.

159
00:14:21,365 --> 00:14:25,422
Rasool Allah ﷺ says there's a difference between the shepherds of camels and the shepherds of sheep,

160
00:14:26,897 --> 00:14:29,965
you could've are affected by even the line of work that you do.

161
00:14:30,696 --> 00:14:33,869
The shepherd's of camels because they're dealing with arrogant animals,

162
00:14:34,548 --> 00:14:36,272
they tend to develop arrogance too,

163
00:14:37,228 --> 00:14:42,100
while the shepherd of sheep because they're dealing with very soft and compassionate animals,

164
00:14:42,394 --> 00:14:44,418
 they become very soft and compassionate too,

165
00:14:45,345 --> 00:14:47,016
and that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

166
00:14:47,182 --> 00:14:49,418
مَا مِنْ نَبِيّْ اِلَّا وَرَاعَ الْغَنَمْ

167
00:14:49,815 --> 00:14:54,318
Every Prophet has been a shepherd of sheep.

168
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:57,384
Every prophet has been a shepherd of sheep,

169
00:14:57,491 --> 00:14:59,896
 they said: What about you? He said: Even me.

170
00:15:00,352 --> 00:15:01,941
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to be a shepherd.

171
00:15:06,441 --> 00:15:11,632
So, these tough men would come into Madina and they were rude.

172
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:15,778
And the Sahabah(صحابه) were getting frustrated by their Akhlaaq(أخلاق).

173
00:15:16,648 --> 00:15:19,398
They didn't have the tarbiya(تربيعة) that the Sahabah(صحابه) had,

174
00:15:19,766 --> 00:15:21,554
and they were complaining to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), the Khalifah(خليفه),

175
00:15:21,579 --> 00:15:24,486
they were saying, how can we deal with these people?

176
00:15:25,115 --> 00:15:26,647
They're harsh, they're rude.

177
00:15:27,783 --> 00:15:30,826
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) had enough, so he stood up and he gave a Khutba(خطبة)

178
00:15:31,852 --> 00:15:39,168
and he called all of the Sahabah(صحابه), he said: You are complaining about these men,

179
00:15:40,365 --> 00:15:44,924
who came into Madina whom, we are going to send, to fight the enemy.

180
00:15:46,350 --> 00:15:47,277
He said:

181
00:15:48,817 --> 00:15:56,819
This harshness and rudeness and toughness in them is going to be used against the enemy of Allah.

182
00:15:59,174 --> 00:16:05,379
So, I ask you in the name of Allah, if you have any duty of respect and obedience towards me,

183
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:11,933
to leave them alone, and to forgive them, and not to be harsh with them,

184
00:16:12,593 --> 00:16:15,659
except, if they disobey the commands of Allah.

185
00:16:17,859 --> 00:16:20,776
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه is saying, overlook their mistakes,

186
00:16:21,983 --> 00:16:24,621
if they are harsh with you, smile on their faces.

187
00:16:25,209 --> 00:16:28,709
Why? Because this harshness that they have

188
00:16:29,013 --> 00:16:32,221
is going to be Against the Adoo(عدوّ) of Allah, the enemy of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

189
00:16:34,768 --> 00:16:37,139
So, even though they lacked the tarbiya(تربية)

190
00:16:37,675 --> 00:16:40,779
but Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was ready to send them out,

191
00:16:40,853 --> 00:16:41,207
Why?

192
00:16:41,247 --> 00:16:47,210
Because he saw that they can use, what they have against Adaa e Allah(عداءالله عَزَّوَجَلْ).

193
00:16:47,317 --> 00:16:49,130
Over here Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying,

194
00:16:49,247 --> 00:16:54,279
Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمرو بن معديكرب) and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) might not be the most perfect and ideal of men.

195
00:16:54,529 --> 00:17:00,703
However, when it comes to the art of war, they are the men you should have next to you.

196
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:03,945
I mean it's, we talked about Amr Bin Maadi Akrib(عمرو بن معديكرب)

197
00:17:03,970 --> 00:17:10,392
we said: That he once held the horse by its legs and the horse couldn't even move.

198
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:15,798
These were strong men and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي), there was one story about him

199
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:23,483
 and this story is most in Siraj ul Mulook(سراج الملوك) by Turtoshi(ترتوشي).

200
00:17:25,569 --> 00:17:35,628
He goes on his own and he enters into the camp of the Persian general and he walks in,

201
00:17:36,566 --> 00:17:45,360
he goes straight, to the compound of the general of the entire army

202
00:17:47,842 --> 00:17:52,207
and he takes the horse of the general and walks out.

203
00:17:53,594 --> 00:18:00,509
So, one of their knights he pursues him, Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي), he turns around,

204
00:18:00,781 --> 00:18:02,751
he kills him and takes his horse.

205
00:18:04,426 --> 00:18:08,735
The second knight among them follows Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي),

206
00:18:08,822 --> 00:18:10,378
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) kills him and takes his horse.

207
00:18:10,402 --> 00:18:15,858
Now, he has three horses, the third knight attacks him

208
00:18:16,859 --> 00:18:21,330
and Tulaiha(طليحه) succeeds in having him, surrender.

209
00:18:21,804 --> 00:18:26,169
So, he ties him up and takes this horse, now he has four horses and one prisoner of war.

210
00:18:26,194 --> 00:18:29,382
And he walks out and he goes to the camp of the Muslims

211
00:18:29,407 --> 00:18:32,878
and hands over four horses and a prisoner of war.

212
00:18:33,664 --> 00:18:38,113
So, this fighter he said: he asked the Ameer(أمير) of the Muslims, he said;

213
00:18:38,378 --> 00:18:44,732
I have one question, please answer it, one question.

214
00:18:44,986 --> 00:18:46,216
Who was this man?

215
00:18:47,687 --> 00:18:48,834
He said, Why are you asking?

216
00:18:48,874 --> 00:18:53,373
He said: I've never seen something like this in my life.

217
00:18:54,061 --> 00:19:01,138
He goes straight to the compound of our leader, which is guarded by 70,000 soldiers.

218
00:19:02,357 --> 00:19:05,607
And he goes straight, and takes away the horse of our general.

219
00:19:07,282 --> 00:19:13,353
And then one man among us, whom we consider is equal to 1000 fighters, was killed by him,

220
00:19:14,329 --> 00:19:21,207
a second of our fighters, who is equal to 1000 was killed by him, and then I went to pursue him.

221
00:19:21,262 --> 00:19:27,137
And I don't think that there's anyone in our army equal to me in strength and courage.

222
00:19:27,504 --> 00:19:30,133
And I have seen death on his hands.

223
00:19:33,069 --> 00:19:35,101
He said, this is Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي).

224
00:19:36,257 --> 00:19:40,742
So, these were men who are good at that field.

225
00:19:41,376 --> 00:19:44,313
But when it comes to other areas, in times of peace,

226
00:19:44,978 --> 00:19:46,837
he said: Put them where they deserve to be.

227
00:19:47,090 --> 00:19:49,591
And that's an important quality of the leader.

228
00:19:50,743 --> 00:19:55,112
You need to know the abilities and the skills of your followers.

229
00:19:55,706 --> 00:19:59,625
Don't expect everyone to be equal, don't expect everyone to do the same thing,

230
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:04,051
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to send the right person to the right place,

231
00:20:04,075 --> 00:20:06,144
he would ask the right person to do the right thing.

232
00:20:07,133 --> 00:20:10,308
When an old man came to the Rasool Allah ﷺ asking him

233
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:14,696
tell me, O Rasool Ullah about one thing, this old man said;

234
00:20:15,164 --> 00:20:17,346
لَقَدْ كَثُرَتْ عَلَيَّ شَرَاعَ لْإِسْلَاْم

235
00:20:18,438 --> 00:20:22,268
The commands of Islam are becoming too many for me to keep track off,

236
00:20:23,225 --> 00:20:25,935
you know, every now and then there's a new Ayah(آية) telling us to do something new.

237
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,320
I can't keep track of all of that.

238
00:20:27,671 --> 00:20:29,607
Tell me one thing that I can hold on to.

239
00:20:30,639 --> 00:20:33,781
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ tell him to do, Go and fight Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).?

240
00:20:34,234 --> 00:20:35,272
No! He told him, zikr(زكر),

241
00:20:35,479 --> 00:20:38,534
zikr(زكر) of Allah, do the Zikr(زكر) of Allah, because this is an old man,

242
00:20:39,019 --> 00:20:42,304
and that's the most suitable thing for him, the Zikr(زكر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

243
00:20:42,776 --> 00:20:44,806
لَا يَذَالُّوْ لِسَانَكْ رَتْبٌ بِزِكْرِالله

244
00:20:44,830 --> 00:20:49,011
Your tongue should be soft all the time moving doing the zikr(زكر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

245
00:20:49,813 --> 00:20:55,048
While when a tough man, young man who is married to nine women came to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

246
00:20:55,211 --> 00:20:58,462
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him first of all, you have to divorce five of your women,

247
00:20:58,907 --> 00:21:00,001
and then go Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

248
00:21:01,642 --> 00:21:04,091
So, different people would be told to do different things.

249
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:07,953
When Noaim Ibn Masood(نُعَيم إبن مسعود) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

250
00:21:07,978 --> 00:21:10,332
I want to join you and this was during the Battle of the trench.

251
00:21:10,690 --> 00:21:12,347
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Don't join me.

252
00:21:12,561 --> 00:21:14,549
If you join me, you're going to be only one soldier

253
00:21:14,573 --> 00:21:17,751
but go and divide the enemy from within.

254
00:21:24,466 --> 00:21:31,482
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is our example in leadership, put the right person in the right place.

255
00:21:36,334 --> 00:21:41,096
Number two, Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) Umar Bin Khattabرضي الله عنه

256
00:21:42,271 --> 00:21:48,269
considered it to be his responsibility to safeguard the Muslims and protect them.

257
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:53,386
There are statements to the extent of him saying,

258
00:21:54,042 --> 00:22:02,184
I wish there was a wall of fire between me and the Romans.

259
00:22:04,873 --> 00:22:08,061
He has taken away Ash-Sham(ألشام), taken away Egypt, taken away North Africa,

260
00:22:09,417 --> 00:22:14,529
now he wants to consolidate, what he has teach them Islam spread the Da'wah(دعوة)

261
00:22:15,855 --> 00:22:22,037
because the issue is not just to expand in territory and to grow in size.

262
00:22:22,247 --> 00:22:25,173
And to become an empire, an empty Empire.

263
00:22:26,326 --> 00:22:31,928
You know, with some of the empires of the past, the objective of the kings was to expand,

264
00:22:32,986 --> 00:22:37,127
to be proud that we have more and more land, day in and day out.

265
00:22:38,142 --> 00:22:39,921
But that wasn't the objective of the Khulafa(خلفاء).

266
00:22:40,346 --> 00:22:43,416
The objective of the Khulafa(خلفاء) was to establish the Deen(دِيْن) of Allah.

267
00:22:43,874 --> 00:22:48,192
So, when they take a land, they want to establish the Deen(دِيْن) of Allah on that land.

268
00:22:48,217 --> 00:22:50,866
What's the point of taking that land if Kuffr(كفر) will carry on,

269
00:22:51,655 --> 00:22:56,071
because some of those areas were very unruly and difficult,

270
00:22:56,579 --> 00:22:59,574
and the nature of the people was difficult in some of those lands.

271
00:23:00,618 --> 00:23:05,640
I mean the Khulafa(خلفاء) had to deal with people like Al-BarBar(ألبربر), like Khurasaan(خراسان)

272
00:23:06,003 --> 00:23:09,015
like different nations like Persia, like Al-Akraad(ألأكراد),

273
00:23:09,285 --> 00:23:11,554
you're talking about a multi ethnic Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

274
00:23:11,586 --> 00:23:14,322
it wasn't all just one ethnic group, it wasn't all Arabs.

275
00:23:14,651 --> 00:23:16,732
In the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), you had Arabs,

276
00:23:17,078 --> 00:23:24,964
you had Persians, you had Kurds, you had Indians, you had the Turkish people,

277
00:23:25,784 --> 00:23:31,273
you had Barbar, different languages, the Coptic's of Egypt,

278
00:23:31,297 --> 00:23:33,875
the people of Egypt were called the about the Acbaat(أكبات), the Copts.

279
00:23:34,518 --> 00:23:38,252
So, it was a multi ethnic Khilafah(خِلَافَه) with different religions.

280
00:23:38,494 --> 00:23:43,485
So, now it is time to consolidate this and to establish the Deen(دِيْن) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on these areas.

281
00:23:43,704 --> 00:23:46,406
And some of these areas are very rebellious, like for example,

282
00:23:46,431 --> 00:23:49,722
the land of Khurasan(خراسان) and Afghanistan, rebelled three times against the Khulafaa(خلفاء)

283
00:23:50,226 --> 00:23:52,894
and whenever, they would invade the land, they would break free again,

284
00:23:52,918 --> 00:23:56,911
they would be taken again and then they would break free and these rebellions carried on,

285
00:23:57,286 --> 00:24:01,126
until eventually Islam sunk in their hearts but it took some time.

286
00:24:02,091 --> 00:24:05,874
It's not like they just opened it and suddenly everybody just became Muslim and that was it.

287
00:24:06,283 --> 00:24:09,611
The Sahabah(صحابه) suffered a lot, they went through a lot of hardship,

288
00:24:10,059 --> 00:24:11,527
to bring these people to Islam.

289
00:24:11,824 --> 00:24:15,898
And that's why Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) it is the manifestation of the Hadith(حديث)

290
00:24:16,098 --> 00:24:18,954
that some people will be brought into Jannah(جنة), in chains.

291
00:24:19,472 --> 00:24:21,576
This is an authentic Hadith(حديث). Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

292
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:24,596
Some people will be brought into Jannah(جنة) in chains.

293
00:24:24,936 --> 00:24:27,801
It wasn't an easy process, they had to be dragged into it.

294
00:24:33,478 --> 00:24:35,688
And sometimes, you would have ethnic problems,

295
00:24:36,227 --> 00:24:38,677
the Arabs fighting with the Barbar in Andalus(أندلس).

296
00:24:39,696 --> 00:24:43,230
And the yemeni tribes fighting with the Seera(سيره) tribes in Khurasan(خراسان)

297
00:24:43,255 --> 00:24:44,283
and also in an Andalus(أندلس).

298
00:24:44,952 --> 00:24:48,212
And all of those problems need to be tackled and countered.

299
00:24:48,581 --> 00:24:51,683
It's not like suddenly they became Muslim and they forgot about all of the Assabiyaat(عصابيات),

300
00:24:51,708 --> 00:24:53,655
they became perfect and ideal human beings.

301
00:24:53,988 --> 00:24:58,850
The process of changing a human being is the most difficult process, and it takes a long time.

302
00:24:59,045 --> 00:25:02,631
That's why the most difficult job of all, is the job of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

303
00:25:03,591 --> 00:25:05,446
because they are dealing with the human heart.

304
00:25:06,567 --> 00:25:08,670
And the human being is the most complicated being.

305
00:25:10,325 --> 00:25:13,742
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن خطاب) said: I wish there was a wall of fire between me and the Romans.

306
00:25:16,536 --> 00:25:19,049
So, he wanted to protect the Muslims.

307
00:25:19,277 --> 00:25:24,093
And now these new people, who just joined the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه)

308
00:25:24,617 --> 00:25:26,703
and embraced Islam, like the people have Ash-Sham(ألشام),

309
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:28,592
the people of Iraq, the people of Khurasaan(خراسان),

310
00:25:28,885 --> 00:25:32,955
it's now the duty of the Khalifah(خليفه) to protect them, yesterday, they were enemies.

311
00:25:33,159 --> 00:25:36,464
Now, it is the responsibility of the Khalifah(خليفه) to protect them, when they're Muslim

312
00:25:36,488 --> 00:25:38,366
or even when they're non Muslim paying Jizya(جزية).

313
00:25:40,533 --> 00:25:47,493
And this is when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) started opening up the sughoor(ثغور),

314
00:25:47,518 --> 00:25:48,745
what is called As-Sughoor(ألثّغور),

315
00:25:49,689 --> 00:25:55,411
As-Sughur(ألثّغر) is a town of Ribaat(رباط) or a fortress,

316
00:25:55,973 --> 00:26:00,126
 it is an army that is dedicated for Ribaat(رباط).

317
00:26:00,610 --> 00:26:02,070
What Ribaat(رباط) means?

318
00:26:03,189 --> 00:26:07,082
You have this frontier land that is between the land of the Daar-Ul-Islam(دارالإسلام) and Daar Ul-Kuffr(دارالاكفر),

319
00:26:07,185 --> 00:26:09,564
 you have the land of Islam and the land of Kuffr(كفر)

320
00:26:10,064 --> 00:26:14,569
that border that frontier land, it needs to be protected and guarded.

321
00:26:15,579 --> 00:26:20,388
The people who are protecting that frontier are called Murabitoon(مرابطون).

322
00:26:21,722 --> 00:26:25,171
And the towns in which they settle in our call Sughoor(ألثّغور).

323
00:26:26,863 --> 00:26:29,718
Al-Basra(ألبصره) was a sughar(ألثّغر), Al-Kufa(ألكوفه) was a sughar(ألثّغر),

324
00:26:30,035 --> 00:26:31,201
Al-Fustat(ألفستات) was a sughar(ألثّغر),

325
00:26:31,285 --> 00:26:36,222
 I mean these towns which are now huge towns, were initially military camps

326
00:26:37,261 --> 00:26:48,975
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would ask his governors to relocate entire tribes into these towns,

327
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:54,209
and the sole purpose of that relocation is to serve as guards Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

328
00:26:55,365 --> 00:26:57,712
Why? Because of the virtues of Ribaat(رباط).

329
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:04,596
Rasool Allah ﷺ says one day spent in Ribaat(رباط)

330
00:27:05,104 --> 00:27:08,393
is greater than 60 years of Sayyam(صيام) and Qayyam(قيام).

331
00:27:09,658 --> 00:27:13,302
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says: One day spent in Ribaat(رباط)

332
00:27:13,471 --> 00:27:16,898
is better than Aetiqaaf(إعتكاف) in Al-Masjid-ul-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام)

333
00:27:20,212 --> 00:27:22,937
because of the virtues of Ribaat(رباط) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

334
00:27:23,774 --> 00:27:31,279
these tribes were willing to relocate and move with their families into these new frontier towns.

335
00:27:31,638 --> 00:27:36,051
They left their homeland, they left their homes, they left their businesses,

336
00:27:36,312 --> 00:27:41,790
and they relocated to new areas, just for the sake of protecting the rest of the Muslims.

337
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:49,322
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه he told Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص).

338
00:27:49,399 --> 00:27:52,472
أُذْقُوْ حُرَّاسَقَ عَلى أَسْكَرَقْ

339
00:27:53,016 --> 00:27:56,171
Spread the guards around your soldiers,

340
00:27:57,142 --> 00:27:59,007
وَتَيَقَّذْ مِنَ الْبِيَاتْ

341
00:27:59,369 --> 00:28:04,099
And beware of nightly attacks, Al-Baiyat(ألبيات) is an attack at night.

342
00:28:05,830 --> 00:28:10,341
And this was an old form of warfare, they would ambush at night

343
00:28:10,381 --> 00:28:14,789
and they would kill everyone because at night you can't really tell the difference between man, woman or child.

344
00:28:15,559 --> 00:28:17,400
So, there was Baiyat(ألبيات) going on both sides,

345
00:28:17,686 --> 00:28:21,488
the Muslims doing Baiyat(ألبيات) to the enemy and the enemy doing bayaat to the Muslims.

346
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:24,838
And this was a very dangerous thing because everybody just gets killed,

347
00:28:25,061 --> 00:28:28,803
attacks at night, you can't really distinguish between civilian and non civilian.

348
00:28:29,131 --> 00:28:33,091
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is telling him, be careful, beware of Baiyat(ألبيات).

349
00:28:34,037 --> 00:28:34,742
And then he said;

350
00:28:34,904 --> 00:28:39,989
وَلَا تُعْتَ بِأَسِيْرِ الَّيْسَ الْعَقْدَ إِلَّا ضَرَبْتَا عُنُقَ لِتُرْهِبَهْ بِذَلِكَ عَدُوْالله وَعَدُوَّكْ

351
00:28:40,541 --> 00:28:47,506
And any prisoner of war that lands in your hand and doesn't have a covenant execute him immediately.

352
00:28:47,655 --> 00:28:51,057
So, that you would terrorize the enemy of Allah and your enemy.

353
00:28:51,481 --> 00:28:56,745
At that particular stage in the war, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to instill fear in the enemy,

354
00:28:56,809 --> 00:29:00,168
 so he said: All of the prisoners of war should be executed.

355
00:29:00,805 --> 00:29:05,707
This is not a general rule, the Ameer(أمير) of the Muslims has the right,

356
00:29:06,268 --> 00:29:14,088
the authority of either execution or enslavement, or freeing with ransom

357
00:29:14,113 --> 00:29:18,219
or freeing for without a ransom, all of that is up to the Ameer(أمير).

358
00:29:18,244 --> 00:29:20,940
And that's according to the classical scholars.

359
00:29:23,070 --> 00:29:29,294
So, the responsibility of guarding the Muslims is responsibility of the Khalifah(خليفه) or Wali-Ul-Amr(وليِّ الّأمر).

360
