يَكْفِرُهَا أَصِّيَامُ وَصَّلَاةُ وَصَّدَقَةُ وَالْأَمْرُوْ بَلْ مَعْرُوْفِ وَنَّحْيِ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرْ

534
00:43:34,881 --> 00:43:37,666
I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say, that the Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

535
00:43:37,706 --> 00:43:40,031
and Fitnah(فِتْنَه) means trial or tribulation,

536
00:43:40,840 --> 00:43:49,556
the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of a man, in his family, his wealth, his self, his children, and his neighbors

537
00:43:50,548 --> 00:43:56,012
is forgiven through Salah(صلاة), Sayyam(صيام) and Sadaqah(صدقه),

538
00:43:56,352 --> 00:43:58,934
and the enjoining good and forbidding evil.

539
00:43:59,894 --> 00:44:01,000
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

540
00:44:01,326 --> 00:44:09,389
لَيْسَ هَذَا أُرِيْد إِنَّمَا اُرِيْدُ الْفِتْنَةِ أَلَّتِيْ تَمَوْجُوْكَ مَوْجَ لْبَحْرِ

541
00:44:10,518 --> 00:44:12,461
This is not what I'm asking about.

542
00:44:12,989 --> 00:44:16,758
I'm asking about the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) that is like the waves of the ocean

543
00:44:17,997 --> 00:44:21,891
he's talking about the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) that is like the waves of the ocean.

544
00:44:23,764 --> 00:44:29,169
Hudaifa(حذيفه) said: O, Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)! Why do you want to know about it?

545
00:44:30,106 --> 00:44:34,178
Between you and that Fitnah(فِتْنَه) is a locked gate.

546
00:44:36,393 --> 00:44:37,845
You don't need to know about it.

547
00:44:38,401 --> 00:44:42,139
You, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), you do not need to know about that Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

548
00:44:42,401 --> 00:44:46,197
Because there is a locked gate between you and that Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

549
00:44:48,247 --> 00:44:52,753
Look at the amazing question that Umar(عُمَر) asked رضي الله عنه. He said;

550
00:44:55,239 --> 00:45:03,700
That gate will it be open, or will it be broke.?

551
00:45:05,368 --> 00:45:08,668
Will it be broken down, or will it be opened?

552
00:45:11,617 --> 00:45:18,493
The lock on this gate, will it be opened with a key, or will it be cracked open and broken?

553
00:45:21,338 --> 00:45:25,339
Why asked such a question? What's the difference?

554
00:45:26,180 --> 00:45:28,847
You open the gate or you break the gate.

555
00:45:30,483 --> 00:45:33,983
He said: Is that gate going to be opened or broken down?

556
00:45:36,389 --> 00:45:40,534
Hudaifa(حذيفه) said: No! Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) it will be broken.

557
00:45:41,925 --> 00:45:43,039
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

558
00:45:43,079 --> 00:45:47,682
If it is broken then it will never be closed again, until the Day of Judgment.

559
00:45:48,920 --> 00:45:49,923
That's why Umar(عُمَر) asked.

560
00:45:51,097 --> 00:45:54,069
If you open a door you can close it, you can shut it,

561
00:45:54,601 --> 00:45:57,521
but if you break it, that's it is broken, forget

562
00:45:58,555 --> 00:46:00,626
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to know, what will happen?

563
00:46:00,658 --> 00:46:04,912
Hudaifa(حذيفه) said: That it will be broken.

564
00:46:05,408 --> 00:46:11,456
Therefore, this gate of Fittan(فتن) will never be closed, until the day of judgment,

565
00:46:12,050 --> 00:46:16,697
the floodgates are open and that will carry on, until the day of judgment,

566
00:46:17,369 --> 00:46:18,405
and that is what happened.

567
00:46:21,815 --> 00:46:24,888
As long as Umar(عُمَر) is alive, there are no Fittan(فتن)

568
00:46:25,252 --> 00:46:29,583
because the Fittan(فتن) don't dare to show their faces, when Umar(عُمَر) is alive.

569
00:46:30,486 --> 00:46:35,002
If Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) cannot face Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), eye to eye,

570
00:46:35,267 --> 00:46:37,485
how can the Fittan(فتن) face him.

571
00:46:40,916 --> 00:46:45,175
The Taba'een(تابعين) who were studying under Hudaifa(حذيفه) and they heard this conversation,

572
00:46:46,470 --> 00:46:47,256
they said;

573
00:46:48,430 --> 00:46:51,526
Did Umar(عُمَر) know, they asked Hudaifa(حذيفه), they said: Did Umar(عُمَر) know,

574
00:46:51,967 --> 00:46:53,109
who the gate was?

575
00:46:53,911 --> 00:46:56,029
Hudaifa(حذيفه) said: Definitely, he did.

576
00:46:56,585 --> 00:47:01,014
Just like he knew that before, tomorrow is today,

577
00:47:02,443 --> 00:47:08,689
because I have told him, in explicit and clear terms, who the gate was.

578
00:47:11,006 --> 00:47:15,128
Now, the Taba'een(تابعين) were shy to ask Hudaifa(حذيفه) who the gate was.

579
00:47:15,506 --> 00:47:18,465
So, they sent Masrooq(مسروق) one of his close student to ask him the question.

580
00:47:19,170 --> 00:47:21,772
He said: Who was the gate, or what is the gate?

581
00:47:22,122 --> 00:47:24,907
Hudaifa(حذيفه) said: Umar(عُمَر) was the gate.

582
00:47:26,274 --> 00:47:31,115
He was the gate, that was preventing the Fittan(فتن) from coming through to this Ummah(امة).

583
00:47:33,321 --> 00:47:40,120
But as soon as he was killed, that's when the seeds of Fittan(فتن) started growing.

584
00:47:41,550 --> 00:47:47,915
You had the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Al-Qadar(ألقدر), Al-Qadariya(ألقدريه) and Al-Jabariya(ألجبرية),

585
00:47:48,833 --> 00:47:58,170
you had the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of what happened with Ali رضي الله عنه and Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

586
00:47:58,629 --> 00:48:05,084
and the split that the Ummah(امة) breaking into Ahl-Us-Sunnah wal Jamaah(أهل لسنة والجماعة)

587
00:48:05,476 --> 00:48:07,752
and Shia(شيعه) and Khawarij(ألخوارج).

588
00:48:08,847 --> 00:48:11,839
And we can see that that split exists until this day.

589
00:48:12,268 --> 00:48:13,728
That split was very old.

590
00:48:14,046 --> 00:48:18,490
The seeds of it, were in the time of the Sahabah(صحابه), in the time of Uthman(عثمان) and Ali(علي)

591
00:48:19,166 --> 00:48:22,873
and it carries on until, this day and only Allah knows if it will ever end.

592
00:48:24,873 --> 00:48:28,122
The Ummah(امة) was one, was unified, there were no different Madhahib(مذاهب),

593
00:48:28,154 --> 00:48:30,033
there were no different groups in the time of Umar(عُمَر).

594
00:48:31,454 --> 00:48:36,685
But after Umar(عُمَر) that is when you started having groups growing and Fittan(فتن) and Ahzaab(أحزاب).

595
00:48:39,225 --> 00:48:45,044
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was a powerful man who was able to stand as a gate

596
00:48:45,107 --> 00:48:47,287
that prevented any Fitnah(فِتْنَه) from coming through.

597
00:48:48,553 --> 00:48:53,060
Not only Fittan(فتن) made public but if you have any doubts in your mind come to Umar(عُمَر)

598
00:48:53,643 --> 00:48:56,763
and it will straighten them out, like we've seen with that man who was

599
00:48:56,923 --> 00:48:59,999
wondering about the meanings of some of the Mutashabihaat(متشابهات), Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an.

600
00:49:00,253 --> 00:49:01,868
He said: come, I will teach you, what they mean?

601
00:49:05,919 --> 00:49:09,309
That man did not leave except with very clear understanding.

602
00:49:09,786 --> 00:49:12,451
He said: O Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I exactly know, what they mean now?

603
00:49:14,509 --> 00:49:19,274
He told him go, and tell your people, who used to pretend to be a Shaikh(شيخ) for them,

604
00:49:19,603 --> 00:49:27,561
go and tell them that you were seeking knowledge but you got it wrong.

605
00:49:32,574 --> 00:49:35,073
إِنَّ سَبِيْغًا أَرَادَالْعِلْمَ فَأَخْتَعْ

606
00:49:37,201 --> 00:49:38,104
You missed the point.

607
00:49:50,976 --> 00:49:52,613
And Hudhaifa(حذيفه) said;

608
00:49:53,445 --> 00:50:01,228
هَلْ كَانَ قَالَ نَعَمْ كَمَا يَعْلَمْ أَنَّ دُوْنَ غَدٍّ أَلَّيْلَ إِنِّيْ حَدَّثْتُ حَدِيْثًا لَيْسَ بِالْأَغَالِيْتَ

609
00:50:01,908 --> 00:50:05,832
Hudhaifa(حذيفه) said: Umar(عُمَر) knew exactly who the door was

610
00:50:06,228 --> 00:50:08,457
 because I told him in an explicit terms.

611
00:50:08,537 --> 00:50:14,341
So, Hudhaifa(حذيفه) was not speaking of his opinions, he was speaking based on information of the Ghaeb(غيب)

612
00:50:14,366 --> 00:50:16,525
that he knew from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

613
00:50:17,279 --> 00:50:18,041
Because he said;

614
00:50:18,090 --> 00:50:19,045
لَيْسَ بِالْأَغَالِيْتَ

615
00:50:19,934 --> 00:50:22,576
It's not something that is wrong, it's not something that is doubtful.

616
00:50:23,131 --> 00:50:25,026
I told him about things that are certain.

617
00:50:25,624 --> 00:50:30,057
So, Hudhaifa(حذيفه) knew some of Ilm(علم) of Al-Ghaeb(ألغيب) because Rasool Allah ﷺ told him,

618
00:50:31,921 --> 00:50:34,850
and by the way what other secrets Hudhaifa(حذيفه) have?

619
00:50:35,311 --> 00:50:37,783
He knew the names of Al-Munafiqeen(ألمنافقين).

620
00:50:47,028 --> 00:50:50,815
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) used to make a Dua(دُعَا), an interesting Dua(دُعَا);

621
00:50:53,728 --> 00:51:02,322
أَلَّلهُمَّ إِنِّيْ أَسْئَلُكَ قَتْلًا فِيْ سَبِيْلِكَ ، وَوَفَاتً فِيْ بَلَدِ النَبِيِّكْ

622
00:51:03,165 --> 00:51:13,633
O Allah I asked you, to be killed in Your path and to die in the town of Your Prophet,

623
00:51:15,063 --> 00:51:17,237
and then he would ask himself the question.

624
00:51:18,168 --> 00:51:22,742
How can I die as a Shaheed(شهيد) in the town of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

625
00:51:24,613 --> 00:51:28,967
because Madina was the heartland of Islam, no army could reach there.

626
00:51:29,694 --> 00:51:34,693
The land of the Thaghur(ثغور), the frontier land is so far away from Madina,

627
00:51:34,718 --> 00:51:38,248
no enemy could dream of getting near to Madina in the time of Umar(عُمَر).

628
00:51:38,546 --> 00:51:42,696
So, Umar(عُمَر) would wonder, I'm asking a Dua(دُعَا) but how can it happen.

629
00:51:43,769 --> 00:51:46,565
In fact, his daughter Hafsa(حفصه) would ask him, she say: O my father,

630
00:51:46,869 --> 00:51:49,769
what do you mean dying as a Shaheed(شهيد) in Madina. How can that happen?

631
00:51:51,422 --> 00:51:53,031
But then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would say;

632
00:51:53,609 --> 00:51:56,597
If Allah wants it to happen, He will make it happen.

633
00:51:57,781 --> 00:52:03,973
And this tells you if you want something from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, ask Allah

634
00:52:04,894 --> 00:52:06,777
and if Allah want it to happen, it will happen.

635
00:52:07,443 --> 00:52:10,110
There's no limit to what Dua(دُعَا) you can make.

636
00:52:11,254 --> 00:52:12,879
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was making a Dua(دُعَا)

637
00:52:12,904 --> 00:52:16,463
 that seemed to be very difficult to happen or impossible

638
00:52:17,247 --> 00:52:22,357
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ created the means for that Dua(دُعَا) to be fulfilled.

639
00:52:31,369 --> 00:52:33,064
So, ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ make Dua(دُعَا).

640
00:52:34,135 --> 00:52:40,725
In fact, if you don't make Dua(دُعَا) to Allah, Allah becomes angry with you.

641
00:52:41,166 --> 00:52:44,491
مَنْ لَّمْ يَسَّ الله يَغْضَبْ عَلَيْه

642
00:52:45,661 --> 00:52:48,059
And that's very interesting because if you have a friend

643
00:52:49,520 --> 00:52:52,297
and you don't ask him for any favors, they love you.

644
00:52:53,950 --> 00:52:56,002
If you start asking them for favors,

645
00:52:57,819 --> 00:53:00,700
today you come to him and say, brother, I'm broke.

646
00:53:02,036 --> 00:53:05,601
I want to borrow 10 quid that's it, just 10 quid.

647
00:53:06,030 --> 00:53:08,379
Here we go. Sure, no problem take it.

648
00:53:09,308 --> 00:53:14,154
Next day, brother you know what? I need to 20 quid today, all right, Tayeb(طيب),

649
00:53:14,457 --> 00:53:16,780
what's going on? He said: Well I have situation not good here?

650
00:53:16,859 --> 00:53:17,875
That's it take 20 quid.

651
00:53:18,464 --> 00:53:21,772
Next day, I need 50 quid,

652
00:53:22,756 --> 00:53:26,538
 Come on man you're asking for too much, he gives it to you.

653
00:53:26,569 --> 00:53:27,764
Next day a 100 quid,

654
00:53:29,624 --> 00:53:32,739
that's it brother you're asking for too much you go your way I'm going mine.

655
00:53:33,426 --> 00:53:37,177
I Fed up, frustrated with you, you're asking too much, you're begging.

656
00:53:39,716 --> 00:53:43,149
However, with Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ the more you ask him, the more He loves you.

657
00:53:46,606 --> 00:53:48,703
And if you don't ask Him, He is angry with you.

658
00:53:50,912 --> 00:53:54,608
And that's the meaning of the name of Allah Al-Kareem(ألكريم), the generous.

659
00:54:03,499 --> 00:54:10,461
Auf Bin Malik Al-Ashjaaee رضي الله عنه one of the Sahabah(صحابه), he saw a dream;

660
00:54:13,946 --> 00:54:16,472
رَأَيْتُ سَبَبًا فَدَلَّا مِنَّ السَّمَاءْ

661
00:54:18,382 --> 00:54:22,589
And he saw this dream during the reign of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه ,

662
00:54:23,892 --> 00:54:26,860
he saw a rope coming down from the heavens.

663
00:54:29,166 --> 00:54:36,069
وَأَنَّ النَّاسَ تَتَاوَلُوْ لَه’ وَأَنَّ عمر فَضَلَهُمْ بِثَلَاثَةِ أَزْرُعٍ قُلْتُ أَمَاذَكْ

664
00:54:37,818 --> 00:54:40,980
And people were trying to reach to the rope, but they can't.

665
00:54:41,687 --> 00:54:42,972
And then Umar(عُمَر) came in.

666
00:54:43,823 --> 00:54:47,480
And he was three cubits taller than everyone else and he held it.

667
00:54:48,807 --> 00:54:54,318
So, I said: How come, in his dream. He's asking how come, the answer was,

668
00:54:56,240 --> 00:55:01,741
لَأَنَّه’، خَلِيْفَةَ مِنْ خُلَافَاءِ اللهِ تَعَالى فِى الْأَرْضْ

669
00:55:02,113 --> 00:55:07,425
وَأَنَّه’ لَا يَخَافُوْ فِى اللهِ لَوْ مَطَّلَائِمْ، وَأَنَّه’ يُقْتَلُ الشَّهِيْدَ

670
00:55:08,831 --> 00:55:13,170
Because Umar(عُمَر) is one of the Khulafa(خلفاء) of Allah on earth.

671
00:55:14,510 --> 00:55:21,894
And he fears the blame of no blamer and he die as Shaheed(شهيد).

672
00:55:24,371 --> 00:55:27,292
So, Auf Bin Malik(عوف بن مالك), went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), the Khalifah(خليفه)

673
00:55:27,317 --> 00:55:29,289
because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) used to interpret dreams.

674
00:55:30,714 --> 00:55:34,833
So, he went to him and he told him the dream. Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

675
00:55:36,622 --> 00:55:38,950
Call in Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) came in

676
00:55:39,520 --> 00:55:44,139
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told Auf(عوف), he said;

677
00:55:45,210 --> 00:55:50,335
 Narrate the dream to Umar(عُمَر), just like your narrated it to me.

678
00:55:51,033 --> 00:55:53,007
So, he said: I went on narrating the dream.

679
00:55:53,413 --> 00:55:59,652
Until, I reached to the part talking about Umar(عُمَر) being a Khalifah(خليفه) of Allah on earth.

680
00:56:00,690 --> 00:56:01,623
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

681
00:56:01,697 --> 00:56:03,303
"أَكُلُّ هَذَا يَرَعَنْ النَّائِمْ"

682
00:56:03,627 --> 00:56:05,439
All of this can be seen by somebody, who is dreaming

683
00:56:05,464 --> 00:56:07,154
in other words, he's saying this is nonsense.

684
00:56:08,677 --> 00:56:12,231
This cannot be true, all of this stuff you see all of this in your dream, What's going on?

685
00:56:14,638 --> 00:56:23,498
And he told this man that, this is a lie, this is nonsense,

686
00:56:23,751 --> 00:56:28,017
 don't believe in it and that was it.

687
00:56:30,031 --> 00:56:35,122
Until, Umar(عُمَر) became Khalifah(خليفه) and he went to Al-Jabiyyah(ألجابيه) in Ash-Sham(ألشام),

688
00:56:35,908 --> 00:56:37,284
Al-Malik Bin Auf(ألمالك بن عوف) was there.

689
00:56:39,421 --> 00:56:44,398
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was giving Khutbah(خطبه) and then he called Auf(عوف)

690
00:56:45,551 --> 00:56:49,090
and he told him: Narrate to me, your dream.

691
00:56:50,298 --> 00:56:54,941
Auf(عوف) said: Didn't you disbelieve in it and didn't you tell me not to narrate it,

692
00:56:56,016 --> 00:57:00,513
he said: Yes! But I did that because I was embarrassed

693
00:57:02,094 --> 00:57:05,018
for such a dream to be mentioned, in front of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

694
00:57:06,258 --> 00:57:09,455
you are saying that I'm the Khalifah(خليفه) of Allah.

695
00:57:10,292 --> 00:57:13,748
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want such a dream to be mentioned in front of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

696
00:57:14,963 --> 00:57:15,662
 he was shy.

697
00:57:16,073 --> 00:57:19,033
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) considered himself to be a student

698
00:57:19,058 --> 00:57:24,615
and the soldier under Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and he was never looking up for Khalifah(خليفه) at all.

699
00:57:25,974 --> 00:57:29,409
He never wanted to be a Khalifah(خليفه) he never asked for it, and now he was Khalifah(خليفه).

700
00:57:30,318 --> 00:57:33,702
So, he told Auf Bin Malik(عوف بن مالك) narrate to me the dream.

701
00:57:34,249 --> 00:57:36,355
 So, I narrated it to him, the dream he said.

702
00:57:36,903 --> 00:57:41,636
Well, regarding the first part, that I am the Khalifah(خليفه) of Allah as you can see,

703
00:57:44,775 --> 00:57:51,291
regarding the part that I fear the blame of no blamers, in the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

704
00:57:52,212 --> 00:57:55,039
I hope that, that is what Allah knows of me.

705
00:57:57,121 --> 00:58:00,773
And then the part that says that I would be killed as a Shaheed(شهيد),

706
00:58:01,395 --> 00:58:06,309
How can I be killed as a Shaheed(شهيد) when I'm living in the Island of the Arabs?

707
00:58:07,696 --> 00:58:10,184
How can I die as a Shaheed Fee Jazirat Al-Arab(شهيد في الجزيرةالعرب),

708
00:58:10,962 --> 00:58:13,622
وَاَنَّ لِيْ بِشَّهَادَةْ فِيْ جَزِيْرَةِالْعَرَبْ

709
00:58:14,048 --> 00:58:15,121
How can that happen?

710
00:58:23,207 --> 00:58:30,103
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), said: I'm old in age and I'm becoming weak in strength

711
00:58:30,980 --> 00:58:33,209
and my nation is spreading.

712
00:58:34,210 --> 00:58:36,444
So O Allah take away my soul.

713
00:58:37,399 --> 00:58:40,743
When I am not in state of weakness and deficiency.

714
00:58:43,270 --> 00:58:47,020
In other words Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying that I have reached an age

715
00:58:47,848 --> 00:58:52,158
where I fear, I wouldn’t be able to fulfill my responsibilities.

716
00:58:52,723 --> 00:58:55,211
So O Allah I am ready to go, take away my soul.

717
00:58:57,600 --> 00:58:59,282
And that was his last Hajj(حَجْ).

718
00:59:02,103 --> 00:59:06,383
After 10 years of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), Da'wah(دعوة),

719
00:59:07,503 --> 00:59:13,464
taking care of the weak, the orphan, the poor, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) says;

720
00:59:13,489 --> 00:59:16,249
O Allah take me away, take my soul away.

721
00:59:19,299 --> 00:59:21,901
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) saw another dream and,

722
00:59:21,926 --> 00:59:24,416
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) dreams are amazing you know,

723
00:59:24,441 --> 00:59:30,440
how many dreams have we brought up in this session, this is part of a An-Nabuwwa(أنبوة)

724
00:59:31,286 --> 00:59:34,884
and dreams are the Bisharaat(بشارات) that He gives to the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين).

725
00:59:36,214 --> 00:59:43,815
And the interpretation of dreams was Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, and the Sahabah(صحابه) after him.

726
00:59:44,815 --> 00:59:51,417
And in certain stages in our history and in certain conditions,

727
00:59:52,298 --> 00:59:56,689
there is an upsurge, there's a surge in dreams,

728
00:59:57,827 --> 01:00:00,540
and maybe we are going through one of those times,

729
01:00:00,565 --> 01:00:02,513
when there are so many dreams, going around,

730
01:00:03,720 --> 01:00:09,635
 and I know of, some Shuyookh(شيوخ) in Yemen, who are good in interpreting dreams.

731
01:00:12,325 --> 01:00:15,805
So, they get a lot of people coming to them and narrating their dreams.

732
01:00:16,433 --> 01:00:19,246
See, a person is seeing a dream doesn't know, what other people are seeing

733
01:00:19,808 --> 01:00:21,484
but these Shuyookh(شيوخ) who interpret dreams.

734
01:00:22,245 --> 01:00:25,145
They're hearing it, from the different people

735
01:00:25,675 --> 01:00:29,389
and they're saying that there's a surge in the dreams that people are having,

736
01:00:29,753 --> 01:00:34,027
regarding Al-Fittan(ألفتن) and the events of the end of time and such issues.

737
01:00:35,031 --> 01:00:39,265
So, that's an indication of something, and there's such a rise in these dreams, I mean, now

738
01:00:39,437 --> 01:00:43,336
the frequency of brothers and sisters having these dreams is increasing

739
01:00:45,316 --> 01:00:51,953
 and these are Bisharaat(بشارات) glad tidings that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is giving Ummah(امة), .

740
01:00:51,978 --> 01:00:55,525
good news for the believers and they have different objectives.

741
01:00:55,550 --> 01:00:57,533
Sometimes, it's to give a good news to the Ummah(امة),

742
01:00:57,744 --> 01:01:01,498
sometimes it is to give good news to the certain person, who saw the dream

743
01:01:01,768 --> 01:01:05,086
sometimes, it is to strengthen them, sometimes, it is to help them,

744
01:01:05,500 --> 01:01:08,255
in their path towards Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

745
01:01:09,128 --> 01:01:11,561
So, they have different objectives.

746
01:01:12,565 --> 01:01:19,033
And I talked a lot with the scholars sometimes brothers asking me about interpretation of dreams.

747
01:01:19,264 --> 01:01:21,603
So I take it to these scholars and ask them what it means.

748
01:01:22,019 --> 01:01:26,379
And they feel that a lot of these dreams have good news for the Ummah(امة).

749
01:01:27,323 --> 01:01:31,620
 So that’s good, and obviously with dreams, there are indications

750
01:01:31,645 --> 01:01:33,715
 you cannot take them, as facts

751
01:01:34,207 --> 01:01:38,647
there are indications and you don't really know for sure,

752
01:01:38,751 --> 01:01:43,510
if it was a dream, a true dream or false dream, until after the event happens.

753
01:01:44,797 --> 01:01:49,902
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Shuyookh(شيوخ) have told me about some dreams

754
01:01:50,289 --> 01:01:54,217
that were seen in the past, it is just amazing

755
01:01:54,241 --> 01:01:58,572
as if the person who saw this dream has an open book of the future.

756
01:02:00,104 --> 01:02:05,715
Dreams that were seen years ago about events that are recent.

757
01:02:07,036 --> 01:02:09,911
So Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)  this is an area that is truly amazing.

758
01:02:10,318 --> 01:02:15,861
It is as Rasool Allah ﷺ said this is only thing left of Nabuwwa(نبوة) of Prophet hood.

759
01:02:16,564 --> 01:02:25,918
And the fact that a lot of it is happening now is an indication that there is something going on with the Ummah(امة).

760
01:02:25,958 --> 01:02:29,745
 We asked Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give this Ummah(امة) and to grant it victory.

761
01:02:30,193 --> 01:02:32,433
Not only that, but to make us part of that,

762
01:02:32,657 --> 01:02:35,215
that we'd be part of At-Taefah Al-Mansoorah(ألطَّائفه ألمنصوره)

763
01:02:35,409 --> 01:02:38,094
that will give victory to the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

764
01:02:39,503 --> 01:02:41,330
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) he saw a dream.

765
01:02:42,210 --> 01:02:43,686
So, now, see there's a lot of dreams

766
01:02:43,755 --> 01:02:47,293
because it's coming before an important event and that's death of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

767
01:02:48,411 --> 01:02:51,161
So, there is a surge of dreams, you have many dreams regarding this event.

768
01:02:51,895 --> 01:02:55,535
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) saw a dream he has some horses with him

769
01:02:55,916 --> 01:02:57,567
and then is climbing up a mountain

770
01:02:57,884 --> 01:03:02,773
and the number of the horses is decreasing, decreasing, decreasing until, he had only one left

771
01:03:03,796 --> 01:03:08,170
 and he reaches to a very slippery Cliff but he climbs it,

772
01:03:09,029 --> 01:03:14,820
and on top of that cliff he finds, Rasool Allah ﷺ sitting with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

773
01:03:15,811 --> 01:03:20,626
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was calling and inviting Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to join them.

774
01:03:23,212 --> 01:03:25,235
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) interpreted this to mean

775
01:03:25,260 --> 01:03:28,079
that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) his death is approaching.

776
01:03:29,308 --> 01:03:32,138
So they told Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) tell Umar(عُمَر) about it. He said;

777
01:03:32,566 --> 01:03:36,309
I am not going to be the one, to send his condolences to him,

778
01:03:37,854 --> 01:03:41,747
and he refused to tell Umar(عُمَر) about this dream.

779
01:03:43,947 --> 01:03:45,931
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه saw a dream

780
01:03:46,173 --> 01:03:48,826
and this was the last Khutba(خطبه) of Jumu'ah(جمعه) that he gave

781
01:03:50,080 --> 01:03:54,164
and this is in the Masnad Al-Imam Ahmad(مسند إمام أحمد) and it is Sahih(صحيح), he said;

782
01:03:54,621 --> 01:03:59,611
إِنِّيْ قَدْ رَأَيْتُ رُعْيَه لَأرَاهَا إِلَّاحُضُوْرَ أَجَلِيْ،

783
01:04:00,452 --> 01:04:04,088
رَأَيْتُكَ أَنَّ دِيْقًا نَقَرَنِيْ نَقْرَتَيْنََ

784
01:04:04,673 --> 01:04:08,984
وَ إِنَّ قَوْمًا يَعْمُرُوْنَنِي أنْ أسْتَخْلِفْ فَهُوَ عَيْنَ الّخَلِيْفَةْ مِمْ بَعدِ

785
01:04:09,388 --> 01:04:16,304
وَ إنَّ الله لَمْ يَكُنْ لِيُضَيَّ دٍيْنَه، وَلَا خِلَافَتَه’، وَلَلَّذِيْ بَعْثَ بِهِ نَبِيَه

786
01:04:16,519 --> 01:04:21,322
 فَإِنْ عَجِلَ بِأمرٌ خِلَافَتُ شُوْرَى فَإِنَ هَا أُلآءِ سِتَّهْ

787
01:04:21,512 --> 01:04:24,868
ألَّذِيْنَ تُوُ فِّيَّ رَسُوْلَ الله صلى الله على وسلم وَهُوَّ عَنْهُمْ رَاضِيْ

788
01:04:26,855 --> 01:04:28,894
He said: I've seen a dream.

789
01:04:28,990 --> 01:04:31,291
This was Khutba(خطبه) of Jumu'ah(جمعه) talking about his dream,

790
01:04:31,598 --> 01:04:37,703
he said: I've seen a dream and I interpreted to mean that my death is close,

791
01:04:38,976 --> 01:04:44,341
I've seen that a rooster has pecked me twice

792
01:04:45,762 --> 01:04:49,507
and that some men are asking me to appoint a Khalifah(خليفه).

793
01:04:50,156 --> 01:04:53,828
Now, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will not forsake

794
01:04:54,054 --> 01:04:59,392
His religion or His Khilafah(خلافه) or the message of Muhammadﷺ.

795
01:04:59,925 --> 01:05:05,956
So, if something happens to me then the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is decided by these six men

796
01:05:06,315 --> 01:05:09,495
whom Rasool Allah ﷺ died and he was pleased with them

797
01:05:10,628 --> 01:05:13,660
and that is when he appointed the Council of six,

798
01:05:16,091 --> 01:05:18,579
but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) carried on of work as usual.

799
01:05:20,684 --> 01:05:25,823
He had a meeting with Hudhaifa Bin Yaman(حذيفه.بن يمان) and Sahal Bin Haneef(سهل بن حنيف),

800
01:05:26,788 --> 01:05:32,835
he sent them to survey the land of Iraq and to assess the Kharaaj(خراج) the land tax.

801
01:05:34,741 --> 01:05:37,376
So, when they came and delivered the report to him.

802
01:05:37,528 --> 01:05:41,978
He said: I hope that you did not make it difficult on the people of Iraq,

803
01:05:42,243 --> 01:05:45,552
he is talking about the non Muslims of Iraq, who are going to pay the Kharaaj(خراج).

804
01:05:46,102 --> 01:05:49,496
Umar(عُمَر) was concerned, he didn't want it to be difficult for them.

805
01:05:49,521 --> 01:05:50,925
He didn't want to overburden them.

806
01:05:51,613 --> 01:05:54,945
So, he said: I hope you didn't make it difficult on the families of Iraq.

807
01:05:55,207 --> 01:05:58,784
They said: No, we left them with more than what we take from them.

808
01:06:00,068 --> 01:06:01,807
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

809
01:06:04,068 --> 01:06:14,700
وَالله إِنْ سَلَّمَنِيَ الله لَا أَدَّعَنَّ أرَامِلَ أَهْلِ الْعِرَاقِ، لَا يَحْتَجْنَا إِلَا رَجٌلٍ بَعْدِيْ أبَدًا

810
01:06:14,724 --> 01:06:18,748
لَا أدَعنَّ أرَامِلَ أهْلِ الْعِرَاقِ إِلَا رَجُلٍ بَعْدِيْ أبَدًا

811
01:06:19,412 --> 01:06:26,504
In the name of Allah, if Allah grants me life, I'm not going to leave the widows of Iraq

812
01:06:26,745 --> 01:06:28,921
in need of any man after me.

813
01:06:30,480 --> 01:06:32,580
I'm going to take care of all of their needs,

814
01:06:33,616 --> 01:06:37,061
so that they wouldn't need the help or assistance of anybody else.

815
01:06:38,710 --> 01:06:42,675
Four days after the statement Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was killed رضي الله عنه

816
01:06:43,554 --> 01:06:47,022
and that's what we will talk about In Sha Allah ho Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى) tomorrow night.

817
01:06:47,047 --> 01:06:49,011
And that will be our last session

818
01:06:49,347 --> 01:06:52,772
on the life of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) Al-Farooq رضي الله عنه.

819
01:06:52,923 --> 01:06:55,407
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

820
01:06:55,432 --> 01:06:59,687
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

821
01:06:59,797 --> 01:07:04,003
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

822
01:07:04,027 --> 01:07:08,087
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

823
01:07:08,407 --> 01:07:12,614
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

